        "notes": "Reviewed all three Verification steps and all four cited suppliers. The feedforward Definition permits the scalar acyclic two-layer graph with identity activations and tied weights; its illustrative supplier diagram has all input-to-hidden and hidden-to-output edges in the correct direction. The product-rule supplier applies to bounded scalar multiplication and coordinate projections, yielding continuous partials D_theta Phi=h and D_h Phi=theta, and loss derivative h_2. With fixed x, Dh_0=0 and the direct parameter loss term is zero. Both uses contribute theta^3 x^2, summing to 2 theta^3 x^2. Direct differentiation of (1/2)theta^4 x^2 agrees, including x=0, theta=0 and x=theta=1. No division, branch boundary, AC or approximation-theorem premise. Reader/refuter have no findings. No defect or edit required."
